    double ai_spend_rate; // ai_spend_rate_numer / ai_spend_rate_denom as a double, recomputed per llm_strat_ai_resource_spend_rate_update pass. When the denominator is 0 the function stores the raw bit pattern 0x42a2309c_e5400000 instead of dividing -- that is exactly 1e13, i.e. an 'effectively infinite rate' sentinel rather than a NaN or an error code. Occupies +0x104b0..+0x104b8; the dword at +0x104b4 is this field's HIGH half, which is why the sentinel is written as two 32-bit stores. Named 2026-08-02 (RI-AI); previously undefined bytes.
